Q: How long do lab results take, and what does 'Pending review' mean?
A: Lab results typically take 24 hours from collection, but can take up to 48 in exceptional cases. Pending review is a status that only appears when an AfyaPlus clinician has flagged a result for further discussion before releasing it to the patient record. In those cases, the patient should wait rather than calling the lab directly. Anything that needs clinical judgement goes to an AfyaPlus provider rather than being answered at the desk.
